# Lab smoke backlog

Before starting or proposing lab smoke tests, read and follow
[docs/SMOKE_BACKLOG.md](docs/SMOKE_BACKLOG.md).

- Lab smokes run a PVE free-RAM preflight (`scripts/lab_smoke_preflight.py`)
  before cloning. Do not bypass with `--skip-ram-check` unless the user asks.
  If a prior smoke left running guests, stop/delete them first or the check
  will (correctly) refuse to start more VMs.
- Prefer executing **Open** backlog items in the next smoke round instead of
  repeating only previously green paths.
- After a successful live check, move the item to **Done** with host/VMID/date
  in that file (do not invent results).
- NTP/domain time (`ntp-dc-resync`) stays open until a post–DC-fix smoke
  confirms guest UTC/local time matches reality.
- Do not run another full smoke solely for Recycle Bin / NTP unless the user
  asks or the backlog item is the reason for the round.
